# Smoke test and exactness check: 12 stars (2 real, 10 made up), about 30 s on an Apple M1 (estimated from the 2.3-2.6
# s per star of the 2026-10 reports in NOTES_method_selection.md, not measured on the M1). The threshold is so high that
# every star is written to `out`, so the hash of `out` covers the three numbers of all 12 stars. That is what makes it
# the profile for a change to the arithmetic: build both sides with EXACT=1 (17 digits instead of 6) and "same output"
# means the same doubles. It cannot show a gain from skipping stars that are far from the ISO, because no star is.
# Time grows with the number of stars alone: every star runs 100 clones for 100,000 steps.
iso oumuamua
stars 12
anchors 2
star_seed 20261104
seed_base 1
time_myr -100
steps 100000
threshold_pc 100000
apps cpu
